.TH "UPDATE-BUCKET-METADATA-JOURNAL-TABLE-CONFIGURATION"  "" "" ""
.SH NAME
update-bucket-metadata-journal-table-configuration \- 
.SH DESCRIPTION
.sp
Enables or disables journal table record expiration for an S3 Metadata configuration on a general purpose bucket. For more information, see \fI\%Accelerating data discovery with S3 Metadata\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Permissions
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
To use this operation, you must have the \fBs3:UpdateBucketMetadataJournalTableConfiguration\fP permission. For more information, see \fI\%Setting up permissions for configuring metadata tables\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.sp
The following operations are related to \fBUpdateBucketMetadataJournalTableConfiguration\fP :
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fI\%CreateBucketMetadataConfiguration\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fI\%DeleteBucketMetadataConfiguration\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fI\%GetBucketMetadataConfiguration\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fI\%UpdateBucketMetadataInventoryTableConfiguration\fP
.UNINDENT
.sp
See also: AWS API Documentation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
  update\-bucket\-metadata\-journal\-table\-configuration
\-\-bucket <value>
[\-\-content\-md5 <value>]
[\-\-checksum\-algorithm <value>]
\-\-journal\-table\-configuration <value>
[\-\-expected\-bucket\-owner <value>]
[\-\-cli\-input\-json | \-\-cli\-input\-yaml]
[\-\-generate\-cli\-skeleton <value>]
[\-\-debug]
[\-\-endpoint\-url <value>]
[\-\-no\-verify\-ssl]
[\-\-no\-paginate]
[\-\-output <value>]
[\-\-query <value>]
[\-\-profile <value>]
[\-\-region <value>]
[\-\-version <value>]
[\-\-color <value>]
[\-\-no\-sign\-request]
[\-\-ca\-bundle <value>]
[\-\-cli\-read\-timeout <value>]
[\-\-cli\-connect\-timeout <value>]
[\-\-cli\-binary\-format <value>]
[\-\-no\-cli\-pager]
[\-\-cli\-auto\-prompt]
[\-\-no\-cli\-auto\-prompt]
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH OPTIONS
.sp
\fB\-\-bucket\fP (string) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The general purpose bucket that corresponds to the metadata configuration that you want to enable or disable journal table record expiration for.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-content\-md5\fP (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The \fBContent\-MD5\fP header for the journal table configuration.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-checksum\-algorithm\fP (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The checksum algorithm to use with your journal table configuration.
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCRC32\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCRC32C\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSHA1\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSHA256\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCRC64NVME\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-journal\-table\-configuration\fP (structure) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The contents of your journal table configuration.
.sp
RecordExpiration \-> (structure) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The journal table record expiration settings for the journal table.
.sp
Expiration \-> (string) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies whether journal table record expiration is enabled or disabled.
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBENABLED\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBDISABLED\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Days \-> (integer)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
If you enable journal table record expiration, you can set the number of days to retain your journal table records. Journal table records must be retained for a minimum of 7 days. To set this value, specify any whole number from \fB7\fP to \fB2147483647\fP . For example, to retain your journal table records for one year, set this value to \fB365\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Shorthand Syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
RecordExpiration={Expiration=string,Days=integer}
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
JSON Syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
{
  \(dqRecordExpiration\(dq: {
    \(dqExpiration\(dq: \(dqENABLED\(dq|\(dqDISABLED\(dq,
    \(dqDays\(dq: integer
  }
}
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-expected\-bucket\-owner\fP (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The expected owner of the general purpose bucket that corresponds to the metadata table configuration that you want to enable or disable journal table record expiration for.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-cli\-input\-json\fP | \fB\-\-cli\-input\-yaml\fP (string)
Reads arguments from the JSON string provided. The JSON string follows the format provided by \fB\-\-generate\-cli\-skeleton\fP\&. If other arguments are provided on the command line, those values will override the JSON\-provided values. It is not possible to pass arbitrary binary values using a JSON\-provided value as the string will be taken literally. This may not be specified along with \fB\-\-cli\-input\-yaml\fP\&.
.sp
\fB\-\-generate\-cli\-skeleton\fP (string)
Prints a JSON skeleton to standard output without sending an API request. If provided with no value or the value \fBinput\fP, prints a sample input JSON that can be used as an argument for \fB\-\-cli\-input\-json\fP\&. Similarly, if provided \fByaml\-input\fP it will print a sample input YAML that can be used with \fB\-\-cli\-input\-yaml\fP\&. If provided with the value \fBoutput\fP, it validates the command inputs and returns a sample output JSON for that command. The generated JSON skeleton is not stable between versions of the AWS CLI and there are no backwards compatibility guarantees in the JSON skeleton generated.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
